<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Sallarid Emirate</h1><p class="st-meta">941 CE – 981 CE (approx.) · capital Ardabil</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Daylamite dynasty that briefly ruled Azerbaijan and the eastern Caucasus in the 10th century, part of the so-called Iranian intermezzo between Arab and Turkic rule.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sallarid-dynasty">Sallarids</a>, also called Musafirids, were a Daylamite family from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarom">Tarom</a> in the mountains south of the Caspian. After the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sajid-emirate">Sajid Emirate</a> collapsed, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marzuban-ibn-muhammad">Marzuban ibn Muhammad</a> seized <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> in 941, taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardabil">Ardabil</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> and extending his authority to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/caucasian-albania">Arran</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/shirvanshah-state">Shirvan</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/armenia">Armenia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Marzuban ruled through Daylamite soldiers and local governors and drew tribute from Armenian and Albanian princes and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/shirvanshah-state">Shirvanshahs</a>. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sallarid-dynasty">Sallarids</a> were Ismaili-leaning Shiites ruling a largely <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> population. In 943-944 Rus raiders seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barda">Barda</a>, and Marzuban besieged them until disease and his forces drove them out.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Marzuban was captured by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/buyid-dynasty">Buyids</a> in 948, and after his death in 957 his sons fought among themselves. Local Kurdish and Arab dynasties broke away, and around 981 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/rawwadid-emirate">Rawwadid Emirate</a> took over their remaining lands in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 941 CE – 981 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Caucasus</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:78.43%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>941 CE – 981 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ardabil</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Marzuban ibn Muhammad, Ibrahim ibn Marzuban</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Shia Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Persian; Daylami</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a>, <a href="/countries/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sallarids, Musafirids, Langarids</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=961&amp;focus=sallarid-emirate" aria-label="Sallarid Emirate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5882 804 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sallarid Emirate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6202 1060L6156 1088M6202 1060L6153 1065M6202 1060L6136 981"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6156 1088h0M6153 1065h0M6136 981h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6202 1060h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6202 1060h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ardabil. <a href="/atlas?year=961&amp;focus=sallarid-emirate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
